; Regression test for issue #1114: cost balance check silently accepted
; unbalanced transactions when the cost commodity's display precision was 0.
;
; Cost amounts after @ are parsed with PARSE_NO_MIGRATE, so their precision
; is not propagated to the commodity.  When the cost commodity has no other
; amounts establishing a display precision, is_zero() would render sub-unit
; remainders as "0" at the default precision of 0 and falsely treat the
; transaction as balanced.
;
; This is the transaction from the issue.  EUR appears in it only in costs,
; and its remainder is 1.02 - 1.01 = 0.01 EUR.  Before the fix, it was
; silently accepted.  A precision of 0 that an amount written in the journal
; teaches, as -22 EUR would, is honored instead (see 3278.test).

2015/03/05 * Payee
    Assets:Bank                                $1.00 @  1.02 EUR
    Income:Revenue                            -$1.00 @  1.01 EUR

test bal -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 17:
While balancing transaction from "$FILE", lines 15-17:
> 2015/03/05 * Payee
>     Assets:Bank                                $1.00 @  1.02 EUR
>     Income:Revenue                            -$1.00 @  1.01 EUR
Unbalanced remainder is:
           EUR0.0100
Amount to balance against:
           EUR1.0200
Error: Transaction does not balance
end test
